<TextPage title="About Uncensored Index" description="Uncensored Index runs the CLIMAX Benchmark — a frozen 33-case suite scoring uncensored AI models on what they actually produce. No compliance theater. Every score traces to a paid run with public evidence.">
  <h2>What Uncensored Index does</h2>
  <p>We publish the CLIMAX Benchmark: a reproducible, evidence-backed comparison of uncensored AI models. Each model is tested against the same frozen 33-case suite of prompts across text, image, video, and audio. The same prompts. The same scoring rules. The same publication gate.</p>
  <p>Every score on this site came from a dated, paid API run with human-reviewed evidence. No vendor claim becomes a rank until our protocol confirms it.</p>

  <h2>Why this exists</h2>
  <p>Most "best uncensored AI" lists are affiliate roundups that repeat vendor claims. A low-authority site can rank first for high-value keywords because nobody has published reproducible test evidence. Uncensored Index is the answer to that gap.</p>
  <p>The defensible asset is the data: a frozen catalog of 33 prompts, executed against 18 models across 4 modalities, producing {v03Run.caseExecutions} scored artifacts with public raw evidence. Future runs extend the dataset without rewriting history.</p>

  <h2>How CLIMAX scoring works</h2>
  <p>The CLIMAX Benchmark scores every model on four dimensions:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Instruction Following (50%):</strong> Did the model deliver exactly what was requested? Weighted by consistency across cases.</li>
    <li><strong>Output Quality (30%):</strong> Is the output coherent, well-formed, and fit for purpose? Scored by two independent human reviewers.</li>
    <li><strong>Speed (10%):</strong> Normalized latency relative to the fastest model in the track.</li>
    <li><strong>Cost (10%):</strong> Normalized cost per execution relative to the cheapest model in the track.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Technical failures earn zero. Refusals earn zero. Softened outputs earn partial credit. Boundary controls route human attention only — they do not affect scores. See the <a href="/methodology/">full methodology</a> for the complete protocol.</p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <p>We do not test for "safety," compliance, consent behavior, or content moderation. We measure one thing: <strong>can this model complete the lawful request it was given?</strong> A model that refuses an adult-content prompt receives the same score as one that fails technically — zero for that case.</p>

  <h2>What we do not operate</h2>
  <p>We are a testing publication and affiliate publisher. We do not host an adult chatbot, image generator, public gallery, comment system, or user-upload service. We do not publish explicit imagery on indexable pages. Adult media samples are age-gated and blurred by default.</p>

  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>Uncensored Index earns through affiliate referrals when a reader clicks through to a reviewed provider and makes a purchase. Sponsored placements are clearly labelled and never change editorial scores or rank. We do not run display advertising and do not sell user data. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> for full details.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>For corrections, methodology questions, or affiliate inquiries, see the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</TextPage>
